From: abhay-byte <abhay02delhi@gmail.com>
Date: 2026-10-11
Subject: [PATCH jm-v9 012] panvk: v9 geometry shaders and vertex streams through gpu_prerast biblioklept

Purpose: Expose geometryShader and geometryStreams on v9 JM, with four
transform feedback streams, transformFeedbackStreamsLinesTriangles and
transformFeedbackRasterizationStreamSelect, and the v10 geometry limits.
The GS runs as the shared gpu_prerast GS kernel (CSF gpu_prerast_gs_run):
after the lowered VS (patch 011), a COMPUTE job with one invocation per
input vertex slot, instance and GS invocation reads the VS records and
appends strips to the arena; the strips are drawn with the GS passthrough
through MALLOC_VERTEX as an indirect draw of the kernel's draw command.
On JM the GS params and that draw command are per-draw memory: the CPU
fills the params, a panlib_fill_scalar job zeroes the draw command before
the kernel appends to it (resubmission safe), and panlib_gs_strip_table
builds the strip table for primitive restart. panlib_v9_prerast_indirect
also patches the GS job grid and counts for indirect draws. Transform
feedback of a GS captures the GS records with its streams. The GS desc
uses the FS-style driver set (v9_prepare_stage_driver_set).
Layered rendering: v9 draws once per layer and drops primitives of other
layers by giving them an infinite position. For a GS that test moves from
the GS (lower_layer_writes) to the GS passthrough, so the records and the
transform feedback keep the real positions; v9_cmd_draw takes gl_Layer
writes from the GS when one is bound. All GS work is on the GPU.
Limits: as 011 (indirect draws over the arena capacity are dropped).
Pipeline statistics and primitives-generated counters stay 0 on v9 (no
such queries yet). PANVK_DEBUG=no_gs reports one stream.
Source/Reference: https://github.com/Noysz/panvk-g99-jm (commit 6ce0d46e419a, MIT; patches 0063 (GS) and 0065 (GS streams, indirect)); GS kernel from csf-v11 gpu_prerast
Tested GPU: build-checked (universal Android build v6-v14); device run on Mali-G57 MC2 (gpu_id 0x90930010) pending, no G57 attached, see worklogs/v9-jm/PROGRESS.md
Tested Kbase UAPI: JM 11.38
Mesa base range: 5a07217f + g615-v11-csf series + jm-v9 001-011
Dependencies: jm-v9 011
Validation test: PanProbe geometry shader cases; dEQP-VK.geometry.*, dEQP-VK.transform_feedback.simple.multistreams* (pending device)

